IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain

-- g7-fourth-schedule.l4: the Fourth Schedule of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration
-- or Air-Conditioning Systems Law 5785-2025, "types of flammable gases" (the Schedule names section 63(a)),
-- as DATA: 95 items, one list, in the Schedule's own order.
--
-- Written by ENCODER G7.  Imports only `prelude` and `domain`.
--
-- What is encoded here, and what is not.
--   * The Schedule as ENACTED (Sefer HaChukim 3349, printed pages 206 to 208).  The Minister's power to change it
--     by order (section 63(a)(1), last clause) is encoded in g7-commencement.l4; no order is in the sources, so
--     this list is the only vintage modelled and a later order would be a new vintage of the list.
--   * Whether a refrigerant is "listed" is a question about its designation only.  The proviso of section
--     63(a)(1), that the use of the refrigerant "was permitted by any law", is not a property of the list and is
--     applied in g7-commencement.l4 to the refrigerant's own field.
--
-- Where the wiki and the gazette differ the gazette governs (the brief).  They differ at item (66): the wiki reads
-- 170E, the gazette E170 (printed page 207, page image viewed, and line 1222 of its text layer).  The list below
-- carries E170.  Items (69) and (71) carry an invisible left-to-right mark (U+200E) in the wiki and in the gazette
-- text layer alike; the marks are not part of the designation and the list does not carry them.
--
-- The designations are bare (no R prefix) and twelve of them are purely numeric (32, 50, 170, 290, 600, 601, 702,
-- 1150, 1270, 40, 611, 717).  A designation is therefore a STRING, never a NUMBER, and it is compared as text.
-- Its letters keep the case the gazette prints (1132a, 142b, 600a against 440A, 411B, 1234yf and 1234ze(E)).
--
-- Quoted below, by script, are lines 728 to 1015 of inputs/law.wiki: the heading, the note naming section 63(a),
-- the sub-heading "types of flammable gases", and the 95 items, each as its marker line and its designation line.

§ `Fourth Schedule (section 63(a)): types of flammable gases`

