@ref Fourth Schedule, items (1) to (95) (src:728-1015)
@desc One entry of the Fourth Schedule: the number of the item and the designation of the flammable refrigerant it lists, bare, as the gazette prints it
DECLARE `Fourth Schedule item` HAS
    `number of the item` IS A NUMBER @desc The number in parentheses on the item, from (1) to (95)
    `designation`        IS A STRING @desc The refrigerant's designation without a leading R and without any direction mark; letters keep the case the gazette prints

-- The Schedule as a list, in its own order.  Positional construction, with a ruler: the two fields are of
-- different types (a number and a text), so a swap cannot typecheck.
@ref Fourth Schedule, items (1) to (95) (src:728-1015)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Fourth Schedule item`
`the Fourth Schedule` MEANS
    --                                   item, designation
    LIST (`Fourth Schedule item` OF  1, "440A")
