§§ `Whether a designation, or a refrigerant, is listed`

-- Section 63(a)(1) speaks of "a flammable refrigerant listed in the Fourth Schedule" (line 461 of the wiki, quoted here).
-- src:461 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} לעניין ביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר הפועלת באמצעות קרר דליק המנוי {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 4|בתוספת הרביעית}}, ובלבד שהשימוש בו הותר על פי כל דין – שלושה חודשים מיום פרסומו או מועד כניסתן לתוקף של תקנות לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 59|סעיף 59}}, לפי המאוחר (להלן – יום התחילה); השר, לאחר התייעצות עם השר להגנת הסביבה, רשאי לשנות, בצו, את {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 4|התוספת הרביעית}};
-- A refrigerant is listed when its designation is one of the 95, compared as plain text: same letters, same case.
-- Nothing is trimmed, case-folded or stripped of an R, because the Schedule prints bare designations and the
-- domain's own description of `designation` says to compare it as plain text.
-- The tolerant alternative, which ignores case, a leading R and direction marks, is below and is a fork
-- (see FRAGMENT-G7.md, fork F-S4-1).
@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461); Fourth Schedule (src:728-1015)
GIVEN d IS A STRING @desc A refrigerant designation without a leading R and without any direction mark, for example 290, 600a, 1234yf or E170
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the designation is printed in the Fourth Schedule` d MEANS
    any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `designation` EQUALS d) `the Fourth Schedule`

-- The headline test the integrator wires to section 63(a)(1).  "Listed" is a property of the designation alone;
-- whether the use of the refrigerant is lawful is a different limb of section 63(a)(1) and is not tested here.
@ref s.63(a)(1) (src:461); Fourth Schedule (src:728-1015)
@export Whether a refrigerant is a flammable refrigerant listed in the Fourth Schedule of the Israeli Law on work on refrigeration and air-conditioning systems, judged by its designation alone
GIVEN r IS A Refrigerant @desc The refrigerant: its designation (for example 290 or 600a, with no leading R) and whether its use is permitted by law
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a refrigerant is a listed flammable refrigerant` r MEANS
    `the designation is printed in the Fourth Schedule` (r's `designation`)

§§ `The tolerant reading of a designation (fork F-S4-1, not taken)`

-- The designation with every direction mark (U+200E, U+200F) removed, a leading "R" or "R-" removed, and every
-- letter in upper case.  The marks are written by a character escape in the build, never typed.
@ref Fourth Schedule (src:728-1015)
GIVEN d IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the designation with direction marks and a leading R removed, in upper case` d MEANS
    IF   STARTSWITH withoutMarks "R-"
    THEN SUBSTRING withoutMarks 2 (STRINGLENGTH withoutMarks MINUS 2)
    ELSE IF   STARTSWITH withoutMarks "R"
         THEN SUBSTRING withoutMarks 1 (STRINGLENGTH withoutMarks MINUS 1)
         ELSE withoutMarks
    WHERE
        withoutMarks MEANS TOUPPER (REPLACE (REPLACE d "‎" "") "‏" "")

@ref Fourth Schedule (src:728-1015)
GIVEN d IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the designation, read tolerantly, is printed in the Fourth Schedule` d MEANS
    any (GIVEN item YIELD `the designation with direction marks and a leading R removed, in upper case` (item's `designation`)
                          EQUALS `the designation with direction marks and a leading R removed, in upper case` d) `the Fourth Schedule`

@ref Fourth Schedule (src:728-1015)
GIVEN r IS A Refrigerant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a refrigerant, read tolerantly, is a listed flammable refrigerant` r MEANS
    `the designation, read tolerantly, is printed in the Fourth Schedule` (r's `designation`)
